WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.262 --> 00:00:06.720
PAUL YOUNG: Welcome
to Cloud OnAir,

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.470
live webinars from Google Cloud.

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:10.759
We host webinars every Tuesday.

00:00:10.759 --> 00:00:12.300
My name is Paul
Young and today we'll

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.520
be talking about power
innovation for SAP

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:15.840
with Google Cloud.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.000
You can ask questions
anytime on the platform.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.390
Today we have Googlers, SAP-ers,
and customers on standby

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:23.460
to answer them, so ask away.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.364
So let's get started.

00:00:25.364 --> 00:00:27.780
As discussed, Paul Young and
I'm the go-to-market director

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.192
for SAP Google Cloud.

00:00:29.192 --> 00:00:30.900
You'll hear plenty
from me, so let's move

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.220
on to the people that matter.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.780
Next to me here is
Isabell Petzelt,

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:36.657
global vice president of SAP
Cloud Platform, go-to-market.

00:00:36.657 --> 00:00:38.490
How do you even fit
that on a business card?

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:39.073
I want to ask.

00:00:39.073 --> 00:00:40.860
We'll just move on from there.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:44.160
Extra weight business
cards for your job titles.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.970
Subject of the
day, first of all,

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:48.940
is SAP Google Cloud partnership.

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:52.170
Especially around SAP Cloud
Platform but in general, too.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.540
Secondly, we have a customer
perspective with METRO.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:56.880
Just great, Axel
Koss from METRO will

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.577
be talking about their
deployment and the decision

00:00:59.577 --> 00:01:00.660
criteria and how we do it.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.250
Just fantastic content.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:05.257
And then lastly, we'll have
a conversation about running

00:01:05.257 --> 00:01:06.090
SAP on Google Cloud.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:08.070
And the things we're
doing to make Google Cloud

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:10.214
the best place
possible to run SAP.

00:01:10.214 --> 00:01:11.880
And, at the end of
that, hopefully we'll

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.590
have time to fit in some
questions and answers as well.

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:18.840
So all that said, let's
get started with topic one.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:20.070
Welcome, Isabell.

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:20.730
ISABELL PETZELT:
Thank you, Paul.

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:21.960
PAUL YOUNG: So do you
want to introduce yourself

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.024
to the people, won't you?

00:01:23.024 --> 00:01:24.190
ISABELL PETZELT: Absolutely.

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:27.840
Isabell Petzelt. I run the
global centers of expertise

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.200
for SAP Cloud Platform.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.940
That's why the name's so along.

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:33.210
So I work a lot with
customers around the globe

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:37.170
in helping them transition
their core enterprise

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:39.000
application into the cloud.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.040
PAUL YOUNG: Great.

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:41.164
Thank you for coming along.

00:01:41.164 --> 00:01:42.873
And you're a long-time
SAP person, right?

00:01:42.873 --> 00:01:44.414
ISABELL PETZELT:
[? 60 ?] plus years.

00:01:44.414 --> 00:01:45.410
Still running strong.

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:47.910
PAUL YOUNG: That's always good.

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:49.607
So what's top of mind?

00:01:49.607 --> 00:01:51.690
What's the challenges that
actually your customers

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:52.450
have right now?

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:53.408
ISABELL PETZELT: Right.

00:01:53.408 --> 00:01:56.235
So what customers are really
challenged about today

00:01:56.235 --> 00:01:58.650
is fundamentally different
than what happened

00:01:58.650 --> 00:01:59.790
in the last few decades.

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:02.250
And SAP traditionally
was focused on really

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:05.610
about standardizing, optimizing
core business processes.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:07.770
But today customers
are really forced

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:10.560
to innovate and
differentiate themselves

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.230
with disruptive business models,
with complete new customer

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:15.300
experiences.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:19.430
Also, giving employees
more purpose in their work,

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:23.160
where they leverage a lot
of technologies and data

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.470
to really solve
those challenges.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.960
And what we see in the most
successful companies-- what

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.840
they are doing-- they are
adopting new technologies

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:33.220
and leveraging
data very quickly.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:35.760
And that is what is delivering
really game-changing outcomes

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:36.260
for them.

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:39.870
Because first, they achieve
a step change in productivity

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:42.870
by applying technologies
like machine learning,

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:46.350
like artificial intelligence
to those core business

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:49.230
processes to automate them
to make them more efficient.

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:51.810
Second, they also redefine
the customer experience

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.460
because it's not
only about anymore

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:55.230
responding to customer needs.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:59.040
It is about predicting what
customers want and create

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:02.230
that satisfaction before
the customers even know it.

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:05.430
And third, it's really about
transforming their employee

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:05.970
engagement.

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:09.600
Because employees want to
have more purpose from work.

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:12.660
They automate certain tasks
so employees can really

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:16.050
focus on higher
level value-adding

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:19.690
activities and tasks to really
move the company forward.

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:21.720
And that is what we
really talk about

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.700
and what we mean with
intelligent enterprise

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:26.370
because customers today
are hungry for innovation,

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:27.537
to differentiate themselves.

00:03:27.537 --> 00:03:28.453
PAUL YOUNG: All right.

00:03:28.453 --> 00:03:31.120
Again, I hear the intelligent
enterprise conversation a lot.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:33.060
And I think that's a
really powerful way

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.170
to explain it, right?

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:36.540
So it's not just about
analytics, a certain one thing.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:38.880
It is about that complete
package for the customer.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:39.690
Very cool.

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:44.280
So what's SAP doing to deliver
against those challenges?

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:45.690
Great idea.

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:46.690
What do we do to fix it?

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:47.130
ISABELL PETZELT: Exactly.

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:48.090
Great idea.

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:51.670
So I said, customers are
really forced to differentiate.

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:55.166
But they want to build that
innovation on a solid trusted

00:03:55.166 --> 00:03:56.790
environment that, on
the one hand side,

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:59.820
gives them the flexibility but
at the other hand side, still

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:03.870
has that robustness and security
to run their core applications.

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:06.720
Because that is what customers
love and trust about SAP--

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.630
running that solid core.

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:11.460
And that is where also SAP
has that process heritage.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:14.700
But now customers really want
to build new functionality

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:18.000
on top of those core processes
to really differentiate

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:18.510
themselves.

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:20.730
Look what happened last
week with Cyber Monday,

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:23.790
where everyone went crazy
here in US shopping,

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:26.040
where retailers
actually launched

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:29.400
a very specific set
of functionality

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:32.910
on their digital platforms
to create a new customer

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:36.030
experience, to launch
specific promotions,

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:39.030
to engage differently with
customers to boost up sales.

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:42.240
You don't want to build those
extensions that only are there

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:45.810
for a week or two into your
core business applications.

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:48.390
You want to build them
side-by-side on a platform also

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:51.570
utilizing latest technologies--
like machine learning

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:52.410
and so on--

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:53.730
to create that experience.

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:56.130
And that is what SAP both
delivers-- on the one hand

00:04:56.130 --> 00:05:00.050
side, solid packaged
applications

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:02.690
for the core business
processes and a platform

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:04.940
to deliver and build
those innovations on top,

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:08.450
and everything in a
single environment.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:11.002
PAUL YOUNG: So I spent a long
time as a customer of SAP,

00:05:11.002 --> 00:05:12.210
actually running SAP systems.

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:13.760
I spent a long time with SAP.

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:16.410
I'll tell you, the point where
it came over to Google Cloud,

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:19.532
the thing that amazed me
was, I think, day three.

00:05:19.532 --> 00:05:20.990
I walked in a room
where there were

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:25.160
20 engineers working on a
single joint project, right?

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:29.900
Amazing alignment and investment
between Google and SAP

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:32.040
to deliver something
that's much more than just,

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:34.700
hey, you can run SAP on
Google Cloud hardware.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:37.580
So do you want to talk quickly
on your perspective on how

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:39.380
Google Cloud and SAP
are working together

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:42.800
to take this far beyond just
another place you can run,

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:43.384
execute Cloud.

00:05:43.384 --> 00:05:44.550
ISABELL PETZELT: Absolutely.

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:46.400
I think that the
partnership between Google

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:48.800
is as fundamental
in a game changer

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:52.280
because together we are helping
our customers in their mission

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:54.650
to succeed in the
digital transformation.

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:58.130
Because I think there are
two fundamental things

00:05:58.130 --> 00:06:00.500
that the teams have delivered.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:02.720
First, they really
created, as you just

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:07.700
said, a fantastic place to
run SAP applications on top

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:08.880
of Google Cloud.

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:11.900
But really optimizing SAP
apps to run on Google Cloud.

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:14.600
But also optimized Google
Cloud to run as apps.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:16.370
So those engineering
initiatives are

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:20.600
happening on both sides for the
maximum efficiency and scale.

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:23.270
So look what we've done with
the virtual machines for HANA,

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:24.530
starting with a few terabytes.

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:26.990
And now you can deploy
16, 18 terabytes

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:28.270
at the snap of a finger.

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:31.970
So that was really the one
piece to create the best

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:34.340
place to run SAP applications.

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:36.140
But what is even
more game changing,

00:06:36.140 --> 00:06:37.910
as we spoke before--
customers want

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:39.470
to build new functionality.

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:41.240
They want to use
latest technology.

00:06:41.240 --> 00:06:43.490
And that is why that move--

00:06:43.490 --> 00:06:47.300
having SAP Cloud Platform
run on Google Cloud--

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:50.480
was a fundamental game changer
because now customers can

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:53.510
consume cutting-edge
technologies from Google--

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.090
be it machine learning,
be it TensorFlow models--

00:06:56.090 --> 00:07:01.670
and really apply and infuse them
into the core processes of SAP

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:05.420
in building those
differentiating innovations

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:06.510
right out of the box.

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:08.630
So we do all the
plumbing for them.

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:11.430
They can really focus on
building the innovation.

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:13.972
And that is what really builds
those intelligent enterprises.

00:07:13.972 --> 00:07:16.596
PAUL YOUNG: It's incredibly cool
if you follow through as well.

00:07:16.596 --> 00:07:19.130
I think this development
where Google fits in the world

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:22.100
is that, if you look at sort
of what we're looking at,

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:24.001
we're also providing data sets.

00:07:24.001 --> 00:07:26.000
I'm here with the stuff
just Cloud for marketing

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.015
where we have the
live analysis of what

00:07:28.015 --> 00:07:29.640
our customers'
advertised this morning.

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:30.650
Are people responding to it?

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:32.420
The ability to,
through Cloud Platform,

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:36.304
to join that through and just
power at a level of granularity

00:07:36.304 --> 00:07:38.720
and a level of detail and a
level of execution that's just

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:39.990
never been achieved before.

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:43.100
That's much, much
more than just a place

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:44.120
to run SAP in the Cloud.

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:45.120
ISABELL PETZELT: Exactly

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:46.390
PAUL YOUNG: Very cool.

00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:48.890
So your favorite
subject, Cloud Platform,

00:07:48.890 --> 00:07:50.071
obviously fits into this.

00:07:50.071 --> 00:07:50.820
Give us the drill.

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:53.000
How does Cloud Platform
bind all of this together?

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:53.870
ISABELL PETZELT: Absolutely.

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:55.310
Cloud Platform is
almost the glue

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:56.435
that's the centerpiece of--

00:07:56.435 --> 00:07:58.268
PAUL YOUNG: Not that
you're biased about it.

00:07:58.268 --> 00:07:59.420
ISABELL PETZELT: No.

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:01.520
Because customers really,
on the one hand side,

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:02.936
they need those
business services.

00:08:02.936 --> 00:08:04.220
They need those processes.

00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:07.670
And they need the innovation or
the infrastructure technology

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:11.570
services from Google Cloud
to really extend their core

00:08:11.570 --> 00:08:14.360
processes in the
SAP applications

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:17.480
with those technologies and
really combine, as I just said,

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:19.730
transactional data
with other sources

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:22.700
that come from Google,
from wherever in the world,

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:24.980
to really change the
customer experience

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:27.320
and really deliver those
disruptive business models.

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:30.350
But they want to do that
on a platform in parallel

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:31.400
to their core systems.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:34.100
So Cloud Platform almost
becomes the bridge

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:36.980
between their packaged apps
and their innovation platform,

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:39.620
the bridge between on-premise
and cloud application,

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:42.230
because it's a stepwise
move, because customers

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:46.520
are moving massive enterprise
workloads into the Cloud.

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:49.370
And they want to do
that at their own pace.

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:51.950
And that is exactly what SAP
Cloud Platform gives them.

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:54.920
It's really the innovation
layer in the cloud

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:58.130
to build intelligent
enterprise applications.

00:08:58.130 --> 00:09:01.790
And that is what is
really the game changer

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:04.340
in the partnership--
that now, SAP Cloud

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:09.350
Platform as the platform, as
a service offering from SAP,

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:11.930
combined with the latest
technologies from Google,

00:09:11.930 --> 00:09:15.530
to extend those core business
processes, while still keeping

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:18.940
the integrity while customers
build those innovations.

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:21.140
And this platform now
runs on Google Cloud.

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:24.749
So that's a game changer for our
customers to build innovation.

00:09:24.749 --> 00:09:26.540
PAUL YOUNG: It's a
really big conversation.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:29.810
I mean, it's fascinating
actually, recently,

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:32.062
how we've seen a huge
uptake in demand.

00:09:32.062 --> 00:09:34.020
Whereas customers start
to plan the [INAUDIBLE]

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:35.936
journeys, and start to
bring [INAUDIBLE] over.

00:09:35.936 --> 00:09:38.370
It's not just, hey, you
know, lift and shift, right?

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:40.120
It's not just pick
it up and drop it.

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:41.015
They want to improve.

00:09:41.015 --> 00:09:41.890
They want to enhance.

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:42.040
They want--

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:42.210
ISABELL PETZELT: Exactly.

00:09:42.210 --> 00:09:43.251
PAUL YOUNG: --to do more.

00:09:43.251 --> 00:09:45.530
And Cloud Platform is how
you unlock that, right?

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:48.290
And again, the objective is
to make it run here, hopefully

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:49.260
better than anywhere.

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:49.750
ISABELL PETZELT: Exactly.

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:50.916
PAUL YOUNG: --to allow that.

00:09:50.916 --> 00:09:54.170
So to that subject,
what happens then?

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:56.540
So customer comes
here, they have SAP

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:57.750
running inside Google Cloud.

00:09:57.750 --> 00:09:59.570
They have Google
Cloud [INAUDIBLE]..

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:00.810
They have Cloud Platform.

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:02.610
What does that do to unlock
the intelligent enterprise?

00:10:02.610 --> 00:10:02.890
ISABELL PETZELT: Right.

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:03.389
Right.

00:10:03.389 --> 00:10:06.260
For that, you need to look at
how SAP delivers innovation,

00:10:06.260 --> 00:10:08.660
or how we deliver
innovation to our customers.

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:10.700
On the one hand side,
in the digital core,

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:13.880
we update that
once, twice a year.

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:17.480
And our cloud applications--
for the different [? LOBs, ?]

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:20.210
we deliver innovations
about once a quarter.

00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:22.620
So any customer gets
that functionality.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:25.210
So they do not really
differentiate themselves

00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:27.100
through those
packaged applications.

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:30.670
So that is probably also not
the speed that customers really

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:35.890
desire when they want to build
those competitive, disruptive

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:38.260
new business models
because they really

00:10:38.260 --> 00:10:39.640
want to innovate rapidly.

00:10:39.640 --> 00:10:40.750
They need iteration.

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:42.640
Sometimes, things
work, don't work.

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:45.430
So they need that
flexibility on a platform

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:49.270
