natural language processing,

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:33.460
and really infuse that into
our core business processes.

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:35.410
Think about the--
we just --released

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:38.920
those event triggers function
as a service for our latest

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:40.510
digital course, S/4HANA.

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:42.700
To give you an
example, I'm German.

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:44.530
I love cars.

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:46.390
And I go now out of
the Google parking lot,

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:48.810
and I take a nice picture
from whatever car--

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:51.250
we are not making
any promotions here--

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:53.680
and post it on my Twitter
feed because it's a cool car.

00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:56.520
Then actually what the car
companies are doing today,

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:59.380
they're scanning the social
feeds using image recognition

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:01.390
to detect their cars,
who has posted what

00:12:01.390 --> 00:12:03.730
about that car on the web.

00:12:03.730 --> 00:12:06.430
And they realize, woo!

00:12:06.430 --> 00:12:09.280
This guy wants to-- is
interested or likes my car.

00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:10.900
Why don't I sent
him an offer where

00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:15.490
he can configure his car,
where he can basically

00:12:15.490 --> 00:12:16.450
submit an order.

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:19.210
And ultimately, I
submit an order.

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:21.160
Then throughout the
production process,

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:25.600
which takes a few weeks and
is running on core solid SAP

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:30.550
systems producing hundreds
and thousands of cars

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:34.390
really at scale, those function
as a service now allow you

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:37.240
that an event gets triggered
when that car enters

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:38.770
the painting facility.

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:41.410
And then a picture is sent
to the customer showing

00:12:41.410 --> 00:12:43.690
exactly his car in the
production line, when

00:12:43.690 --> 00:12:45.174
the seats get in and so on.

00:12:45.174 --> 00:12:46.590
So that keeps the
customer engaged

00:12:46.590 --> 00:12:48.370
with the entire process.

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:51.100
And this is not happening--
or you should not

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:53.260
do that in your
core applications,

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:54.910
because you don't
want to touch that.

00:12:54.910 --> 00:12:57.460
You have to produce
those 200,000 cars.

00:12:57.460 --> 00:13:00.940
